 ## Overview
-Minimal Area Triangulation is a method for decomposing simple closed 3D polygons (isopolygons) resulting from isosurface extraction into a set of triangles, specifically minimizing the total area of the resulting triangles to reduce visual artifacts [S3, unofficial]. It is designed for isopolygons that lie on the boundary of convex octree nodes, leveraging the geometric property that such polygons form simple closed curves on the surface of a convex body [S1, S3, unofficial]. Unlike standard triangulation methods that may introduce edges on cube faces or create self-intersections, this method guarantees a triangulation homeomorphic to a disk, which, for curves on convex bodies, is not self-intersecting [S1, S3, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from siblings like [Marching Cubes](30-isosurface-extraction.md) by operating on the final polygonal boundary rather than voxel cells, and from [Dual Contouring and Surface Nets](6319-dual-contouring-and-surface-nets.md) by optimizing for minimal surface area of the triangulation itself rather than vertex position optimization [S1, S3, unofficial].
+Minimal Area Triangulation is a method for converting non-convex or complex 3D polygons (isopolygons) resulting from isosurface extraction into a set of triangles, minimizing the total area of the resulting mesh to reduce visual artifacts [S2, S3, unofficial]. It solves the inter-slice triangulation problem by finding the optimal triangle decomposition for isosurfaces defined on octrees [S1, S3, unofficial]. Unlike heuristic methods that prioritize speed or simplicity, this method finds the global optimum for the triangulation of a single polygon [S1, unofficial]. It is distinct from [Advancing Front Framework for Implicit Surfaces](819-advancing-front-framework-for-implicit-surfaces.md) which builds surfaces incrementally, and [Dual Contouring and Surface Nets](6319-dual-contouring-and-surface-nets.md) which use optimization to place vertices, by strictly operating on the boundary polygon of an octree node to produce a minimal-area disk homeomorphic to the input [S1, S3, unofficial].
 
